<GuidePage
  title="Property Verification Methodology"
  metaTitle="Property Verification Methodology | DHA Phase 6 Lahore"
  description="A transparent explanation of listing source checks, freshness labels, image validation and the official property checks buyers must complete independently."
  eyebrow="Property data methodology"
  updated="8 September 2026"
  facts={[{ label: 'Source check', value: 'Traceability, not title proof' }, { label: 'Freshness', value: 'Date-based label' }, { label: 'Images', value: 'Local path validated' }, { label: 'Official checks', value: 'Buyer responsibility' }]}
  sections={[
    { heading: 'What “Property Information Verified” means here', paragraphs: ['The verification panel means that required portal fields are present, the source and last-check context are displayed, the availability state can be managed, and the local image reference passes the project validation rules. It does not mean the platform has certified title, inspected original documents, confirmed seller authority, appraised value or guaranteed that an advertisement remains available at the moment you enquire.', 'This distinction protects buyers from treating a software quality check as a legal assurance. The page always retains a source label, property ID and check date so the user can begin a fresh investigation.'] },
    { heading: 'Collection and normalization', paragraphs: ['The current property dataset contains source-referenced records imported from public property marketplace material. Import scripts normalize purpose, property type, sector, size unit, price, status, dates and image references into one schema. Data-quality scripts check required fields and duplicates, while lifecycle utilities determine whether a record is active, reserved, sold or removed.', 'Normalization improves search and comparison but cannot correct an inaccurate statement at its source. A normalized sector name or size should therefore be checked against the exact property documents and physical site before reliance.'] },
    { heading: 'Freshness and availability controls', paragraphs: ['Fresh Listing, Recently Checked, Needs Verification and Verification Required labels are calculated from the age of the last-seen or updated date. Available records appear in active search. Reserved records can remain visible with a warning, sold records retain their SEO page but leave active search, and removed records are excluded according to the lifecycle rules.', 'Dates can become stale between builds, and a status can change without notice. Contact the source or representative and require current evidence before arranging travel or paying money.'] },
    { heading: 'Image and route validation', paragraphs: ['Property images are stored under the public property-image directory and every record resolves either to a validated local WebP file or the local property placeholder. The image validator checks path existence and rejects remote references. Cards and detail pages include dimensions, lazy loading where appropriate and a local fallback.', 'An image confirms only that a deliverable asset exists. It may not prove recency, exact property identity, boundary, included fixtures or current condition. Inspect the property and ask for evidence connecting media to the exact record.'] },
    { heading: 'Checks the buyer must perform independently', paragraphs: ['Before paying a token or signing, confirm seller identity and authority, original ownership documents, exact property reference, dues, NDC requirements, transfer eligibility, restrictions, possession, approved building plans and physical condition through the appropriate DHA Lahore process and qualified legal, tax, engineering or valuation advisers.', 'Use traceable payments and written terms. If ownership involves inheritance, a company, financing, an overseas owner or a representative, obtain specialist advice on the documents and authority required. Current requirements and fees can change, so recheck them near the transaction date.'] },
    { heading: 'Reporting changes and errors', paragraphs: ['A reader can report a sold property, changed demand, incorrect classification, duplicate, image issue or misleading description through the contact channel. Include the property ID and supporting source. Corrections should update the data record rather than only the visible template so cards, detail pages, schema and reports remain consistent.', 'The platform does not guarantee a fixed review interval for every third-party record. The displayed date is the best available indication of when the record was last observed or updated within this system.'] },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    { question: 'Does the verification badge prove ownership?', answer: 'No. It describes portal data checks only. Ownership and transfer eligibility require current official checks and appropriate professional due diligence.' },
    { question: 'Does a fresh listing guarantee availability?', answer: 'No. Freshness describes the age of the stored date. Availability can change after that date, so reconfirm it before relying on the record.' },
    { question: 'Are property images verified as current site photographs?', answer: 'The pipeline verifies local delivery and fallback integrity, not the date or exact identity represented by every source image. Inspect the exact property independently.' },
    { question: 'How are duplicate properties detected?', answer: 'The quality pipeline checks identifiers and normalized property attributes. Similar advertisements can still refer to the same underlying property, so users should compare source details and ask direct questions.' },
    { question: 'Where should official DHA requirements be checked?', answer: 'Use DHA Lahore’s official channels for current ownership, NDC, dues, building and transfer procedures, supported by qualified advisers where appropriate.' },
  ]}
  sources={[{ label: 'DHA Lahore official website', href: 'https://dhalahore.org/' }, { label: 'DHA Lahore property procedures', href: 'https://dhalahore.org/procedures/' }]}
/>
